---
description: Hevy-like workout lifecycle, set completion, recovery, and previous-value rules
alwaysApply: true
---

- The workout lifecycle must match Hevy closely:
  1. Start workout
  2. Add exercises
  3. Log and edit sets inline
  4. Tap checkmark to complete a set
  5. Start per-exercise rest timer automatically
  6. Continue through exercises
  7. Finish workout
  8. Keep workout editable in history
- There can be at most one active workout session at a time.
- A workout may be recoverable after app restart or crash.
- On app relaunch, if an active workout exists, offer Resume / Finish / Discard.
- A completed set remains editable.
- Empty draft rows may exist in UI state, but not as canonical DB rows.
- “Previous” values are derived from historical completed sets, never stored inline.
- Matching order for previous values:
  1. Same exercise
  2. Same set-type bucket if available
  3. Same working-set ordinal if available
  4. Most recent completed set fallback
